From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-system: hide the Plugins page from the System menu

The Plugins page only lists LuCI plugin packages and does not expose
anything useful on this firmware, so keep it out of the left-hand menu.

LuCI only builds menu entries for nodes that carry a title, while the
dispatcher resolves routes from the entry itself, so dropping the title
hides the item without taking the page away.

---
diff --git a/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-system.json b/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-system.json
--- a/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-system.json
+++ b/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-system.json
@@ -98,7 +98,6 @@
 	},
 
 	"admin/system/plugins": {
-		"title": "Plugins",
 		"order": 4,
 		"action": {
 			"type": "view",
